00:13:29.080 --> 00:13:29.480
Well, it was tough as expected.

00:13:29.480 --> 00:13:30.680
What kind of stage is it?

00:13:30.680 --> 00:13:34.650
In the last ballroom dance scene,
Miss Layla and Mr. Yuri

00:13:34.650 --> 00:13:38.790
are supposed to leap on six trapezes one
after another as if they're dancing.

00:13:38.790 --> 00:13:43.090
Wow, that's amazing. What about
everything else?

00:13:54.840 --> 00:13:58.340
You are not in the mood to do anything.
You are not motivated.

00:13:58.340 --> 00:13:59.940
Don't bother telling my fortune.

00:13:59.940 --> 00:14:01.340
As you can see, it's pretty obvious.

00:14:01.340 --> 00:14:04.970
This is also the card that governs creation.

00:14:05.250 --> 00:14:08.770
The road is blocked. But if you want
to see what is up ahead,

00:14:09.080 --> 00:14:11.110
you have to create your own road.

00:14:12.620 --> 00:14:14.060
I have no idea what you're talking about.

00:14:14.060 --> 00:14:16.350
What do you mean by "my own road?"

00:14:18.090 --> 00:14:19.080
I know!

00:14:20.400 --> 00:14:21.790
Is this okay?

00:14:22.100 --> 00:14:23.220
Thanks.

00:14:25.130 --> 00:14:27.340
Are you really going to do it
in a clown suit?

00:14:27.340 --> 00:14:29.800
Yup. If I can't appear on stage,

00:14:29.800 --> 00:14:32.970
I'll just turn the seating area
into my own stage.

00:14:33.240 --> 00:14:35.610
Turn the seating area into your own stage?

00:14:35.610 --> 00:14:36.580
That's right!

00:14:37.450 --> 00:14:41.070
It's great that you always have this
positive attitude, you know?

00:14:42.020 --> 00:14:43.920
Jeez. Ken, you're still here?

00:14:43.920 --> 00:14:46.180
What? Oh, sorry!

00:14:53.860 --> 00:14:56.390
All right, I'm all set!

00:15:08.840 --> 00:15:14.910
Hello, everyone! Are you enjoying
Kaleido Stage?

00:15:15.120 --> 00:15:16.810
Yeah!

00:15:19.090 --> 00:15:22.420
Now, my friends, everyone who wants
a light, gather around!

00:15:22.420 --> 00:15:25.290
You should hurry, or else
the show will start soon!

00:15:28.500 --> 00:15:29.100
Here you go.

00:15:29.100 --> 00:15:29.600
Thank you.

00:15:29.100 --> 00:15:29.600
Here you go.

00:15:29.600 --> 00:15:30.190
Thank you.

00:15:30.400 --> 00:15:31.730
Here. Here. Here.

00:15:31.730 --> 00:15:34.100
Okay, wait a second.

00:15:37.710 --> 00:15:39.230
I did it!

00:15:40.510 --> 00:15:42.480
I finished handing it all out today.

00:15:43.580 --> 00:15:47.010
You have no comprehension
of how the show is run.

00:15:47.280 --> 00:15:49.680
Oh, are you talking about this costume?

00:15:49.680 --> 00:15:55.560
It has nothing to do with that.
Think seriously about what your role is!

00:15:55.560 --> 00:15:58.460
What's wrong?! I don't understand at all.

00:15:58.460 --> 00:15:59.130
Sora...

00:15:59.130 --> 00:15:59.560
What?

00:15:59.130 --> 00:15:59.560
Sora...

00:15:59.560 --> 00:15:59.930
What?

00:15:59.930 --> 00:16:04.330
Just earlier, the show was delayed
ten minutes because of you.

00:16:04.330 --> 00:16:05.200
What?

00:16:05.200 --> 00:16:07.500
You put on a pretty flashy performance,

00:16:07.900 --> 00:16:10.770
so it took a long time to
calm down the audience.

00:16:12.270 --> 00:16:17.180
And, you asked the kids to come out
to get the lights, right?

00:16:17.180 --> 00:16:20.220
Some of them couldn't find their way
back to their seats

00:16:20.220 --> 00:16:22.880
and some were in such a hurry
that they tripped and fell.

00:16:22.880 --> 00:16:25.350
I... I...

00:16:29.490 --> 00:16:30.420
Sora...

00:16:31.990 --> 00:16:36.490
I was only thinking about getting
attention for myself.

00:16:37.270 --> 00:16:40.460
I only cared about getting people
to say that I was amazing.

00:16:41.070 --> 00:16:44.530
I wasn't thinking about the progression
of the show at all.

00:16:45.210 --> 00:16:47.870
No wonder Boss is mad at me.

00:16:50.910 --> 00:16:51.150
Oh! Mr. Yuri.

00:16:51.150 --> 00:16:52.550
It's you.

00:16:51.150 --> 00:16:52.550
Oh! Mr. Yuri.

00:16:52.550 --> 00:16:53.040
Oh! Mr. Yuri.

00:16:53.410 --> 00:16:56.350
I don't want to see a clown cry.

00:16:59.550 --> 00:17:04.510
Even if your heart is crying, isn't it
a clown's job to make people happy?

00:17:05.330 --> 00:17:06.320
Yes.

00:17:14.370 --> 00:17:15.470
Sora!

00:17:15.470 --> 00:17:17.610
Why are you looking like that, Ken?

00:17:17.610 --> 00:17:19.800
I'll help you hand out the lights.

00:17:20.180 --> 00:17:21.210
Thank you.

00:17:21.210 --> 00:17:23.610
No, anything for you, Sora.

00:17:23.610 --> 00:17:29.980
But I'll be fine, because I finally
understand what my role is.

00:17:30.920 --> 00:17:31.890
What?

00:17:35.990 --> 00:17:38.520
A clown's job is to make people happy.

00:17:46.900 --> 00:17:48.560
Sora, what are you doing?

00:17:49.170 --> 00:17:50.540
Oh, Mom.

00:17:50.540 --> 00:17:51.510
What?

00:17:51.510 --> 00:17:55.240
That clown's been standing there
all this time.

00:17:55.980 --> 00:17:57.350
What is it?

00:17:57.350 --> 00:18:01.410
It looks fun. How about this?
Is this a doll?

00:18:01.720 --> 00:18:04.320
I can't believe she's
performing in the lobby.

00:18:04.320 --> 00:18:05.790
She's alive.

00:18:05.790 --> 00:18:06.550
Really?

00:18:06.550 --> 00:18:06.850
No way!

00:18:06.550 --> 00:18:06.850
Really?

00:18:06.850 --> 00:18:07.790
No way!

00:18:08.490 --> 00:18:10.920
The show has already started.

00:18:11.690 --> 00:18:16.890
Even if I'm not on stage, I'm still going
to completely play my role.

00:18:28.840 --> 00:18:30.810
Oh, that's the clown I saw earlier.

00:18:36.720 --> 00:18:38.480
She wasn't a doll.

00:18:38.990 --> 00:18:42.620
Now, I'm here to give everyone
a magic wand!

00:18:43.020 --> 00:18:47.200
Everyone, use your power to fill
the night sky with stars, okay?!

00:18:47.200 --> 00:18:49.160
Okay!

00:18:51.900 --> 00:18:54.240
I don't have a lead role
or anything like that,

00:18:54.240 --> 00:18:56.670
but if I can bring even just a little enjoyment

00:18:56.670 --> 00:18:59.370
to everyone as a supporting character...

00:19:05.250 --> 00:19:06.470
You did it.

00:19:06.850 --> 00:19:09.750
No, I haven't finished yet.

00:19:27.970 --> 00:19:29.530
I understand a little now.

00:19:30.410 --> 00:19:32.970
All roles exist for the audience.

00:19:33.640 --> 00:19:37.080
Bringing these smiles to their faces.
That is Kaleido Stage.

00:19:54.600 --> 00:19:56.230
Miss Layla!

00:19:56.230 --> 00:19:57.250
Miss Layla!

00:19:57.570 --> 00:19:58.530
Miss Layla!

00:20:05.040 --> 00:20:07.440
Oh, you are?

00:20:08.610 --> 00:20:09.870
What is it?

00:20:11.010 --> 00:20:12.810
What? Me?

00:20:13.720 --> 00:20:15.110
You're sure you want me to do it?

00:20:18.490 --> 00:20:23.150
An autograph... Let me think,
how should I sign it?

00:20:29.100 --> 00:20:30.830
Sora

00:20:31.570 --> 00:20:32.560
Here.

00:20:39.640 --> 00:20:40.840
Thank you.

00:20:40.840 --> 00:20:44.510
No, not at all. I'm the one
who should be thanking you.

00:20:45.910 --> 00:20:47.650
Tim, we're leaving!

00:20:47.650 --> 00:20:48.840
Okay.

00:20:53.860 --> 00:20:54.980
Bye-bye.

00:20:58.560 --> 00:21:00.500
Sora, you did a good job.

00:21:00.500 --> 00:21:02.400
I signed an autograph for the first time.

00:21:02.630 --> 00:21:06.130
It would be nice if the boy will cherish
your autograph forever.

00:21:06.130 --> 00:21:07.100
Yeah.

00:21:11.740 --> 00:21:12.800
Kalos.

00:21:13.470 --> 00:21:17.210
I wonder what you're expecting from her.

00:21:28.390 --> 00:21:29.620
What do you think?

00:21:29.620 --> 00:21:31.430
Your autograph is terrible.

00:21:31.430 --> 00:21:33.930
What? Really?

00:21:33.930 --> 00:21:38.570
First of all, there should be a lot of
things you need to practice

00:21:38.570 --> 00:21:40.590
before you practice your autograph.

00:21:41.640 --> 00:21:43.230
That's true, but...

00:21:43.370 --> 00:21:48.070
But I feel like I understand a little bit
of what you said, Fool.

00:21:48.880 --> 00:21:54.250
Creating my own road means
creating my own role.

00:21:54.980 --> 00:21:57.920
And waiting for me ahead on that road
is the audience's smile.

00:21:57.920 --> 00:21:59.850
Are you thanking me?

00:22:00.150 --> 00:22:01.460
Yeah, kind of...

00:22:01.460 --> 00:22:03.460
Then, keep that thought in your heart.

00:22:03.460 --> 00:22:05.620
And now, go take a bath!

00:22:06.290 --> 00:22:13.430
Hey! Like I said, stop blindfolding me!
Hey, Sora!

00:22:15.440 --> 00:22:16.770
You ungrateful wretch!

00:22:21.780 --> 00:22:24.410
<i>When you're lonely, what do you do?</i>

00:22:21.780 --> 00:22:24.410
<i>When you sabishii toki doushitemasuka</i>

00:22:24.410 --> 00:22:26.810
<i>Never say you don't get any of that</i>

00:22:24.410 --> 00:22:26.810
<i>Never say sonna no wakannai</i>

00:22:26.810 --> 00:22:29.720
<i>Sleep, play, flip through a magazine</i>

00:22:26.810 --> 00:22:29.720
<i>Nemuru asobu magazine mekuru</i>

00:22:29.720 --> 00:22:32.020
<i>When you're lonely, you're lonely</i>

00:22:29.720 --> 00:22:32.020
<i>Sabishii toki wa sabishii yo</i>

00:22:32.020 --> 00:22:36.820
<i>Like always, invisible vibes fly around
the city today, tulututu</i>

00:22:32.020 --> 00:22:36.820
<i>Mienai denpa ga kyou mo
tulututu machi ni tobikau</i>

00:22:36.820 --> 00:22:41.460
<i>Anyway, the vector of my heart is
talking about so many reasons</i>

00:22:36.820 --> 00:22:41.460
<i>Anyway kokoro no bekutoru
so many reason hanashiteru</i>

00:22:41.460 --> 00:22:46.170
<i>I want to be free and fly the skies</i>

00:22:41.460 --> 00:22:46.170
<i>Jiyuu ni sora o tobitai keredo</i>

00:22:46.170 --> 00:22:50.840
<i>But I don't have space to spread my wings</i>

00:22:46.170 --> 00:22:50.840
<i>Hane o hirogeru basho ga nai</i>

00:22:50.840 --> 00:22:53.040
<i>But I have faith</i>

00:22:50.840 --> 00:22:53.040
<i>Demo shinjiteru</i>

00:22:53.040 --> 00:22:57.710
<i>There is a future yet to be shaped</i>

00:22:53.040 --> 00:22:57.710
<i>Katachi no nai mirai ga aru yo</i>

00:22:57.710 --> 00:23:02.380
<i>And there's a me that I want to shape</i>

00:22:57.710 --> 00:23:02.380
<i>Katachi ni shitai watashi ga iru</i>

00:23:02.380 --> 00:23:08.860
<i>Even if I'm sad, even if it's a mistake</i>

00:23:02.380 --> 00:23:08.860
<i>Kanashikutemo machigai demo</i>

00:23:08.860 --> 00:23:14.230
<i>I'll do what I want and
fly towards the freedom</i>

00:23:08.860 --> 00:23:14.230
<i>Omou mama fly to the free</i>

00:23:20.230 --> 00:23:22.030
Next Kaleido Star

00:23:22.270 --> 00:23:25.770
I don't want people like you getting up
on the trampoline!

00:23:25.770 --> 00:23:29.880
And so, the three of us end up with
Mia's role as the fairy godmother,

00:23:29.880 --> 00:23:30.710
but Marion...

00:23:30.710 --> 00:23:33.680
She started crying, saying she didn't
want us getting up on the trampoline.

00:23:33.680 --> 00:23:37.650
I heard that Marion's late mother used
to be part of the trampoline cast.

00:23:37.650 --> 00:23:41.820
Maybe I can't appear on stage yet.
Maybe. Maybe. Maybe.

00:23:41.820 --> 00:23:42.960
Next time on Kaleido Star,

00:23:42.960 --> 00:23:43.460
Try Hard and You'll Get an Amazing Chance

00:23:42.960 --> 00:23:43.460
Next time on Kaleido Star,

00:23:43.460 --> 00:23:45.760
Try Hard and You'll Get an Amazing Chance

00:23:43.460 --> 00:23:45.760
"Try Hard and You'll Get an Amazing Chance"

00:23:45.760 --> 00:23:47.850
Try Hard and You'll Get an Amazing Chance

00:23:45.760 --> 00:23:47.850
My wings are my dream
and on towards the sky...
